  "title": "nstime: Add functions to round to a certain precision",
  "description": "Add functions to round a nstime_t object to a given precision.\nNote the existing functions to print a time truncate the to the\ngiven precision rather than rounding. To round, this function\ncould be called first.\n\nnstime_t values do not currently carry an indication of the precision\n(see the comments in #15579), so this explicitly rounds the nsecs value\nas stored. If the nstime_t struct is changed to carry the precision\nas a member, this function would presumably change that as well.\n(That nstime_t values do not carry an indication of their precision\ninternally also means that the printing functions are passed some kind\nof value obtained from, e.g., a file header.)",
